  "prompt": "For each store, what percentage of its 2024 revenue comes from lines priced in cents? These tables may hold errors. A line is priced in cents when its unit_price_eur is more than 10 times the product's unit_cost_eur. A line's revenue is quantity times unit_price_eur minus line_discount_eur, as stored. 2024 means order_ts, as stored, from 1 January 2024 up to but not including 1 January 2025. Return two columns, in this order: store_code and cents_pct, a percentage from 0 to 100 rounded to 2 decimals, missing for a store with no 2024 revenue. Return one row for each store. Any row order is fine.",
